Arguments: {"idea": {
"Name": "infeasibility_frustration_features",
"Title": "Confidently Impossible: Do Interpretable Features Reveal When a Scientific Generative Model Is Fulfilling a Physically Infeasible Design Spec?",
"Short Hypothesis": "When a multi-constraint design specification is physically INFEASIBLE (no valid object can satisfy it), scientific generative models do not refuse or signal failure\u2014they confidently emit a plausible-looking object that silently violates one constraint. We hypothesize the model internally 'knows' the spec is over-constrained: a compact set of interpretable sparse-autoencoder 'frustration' features fire during generation specifically under infeasible specs, and monitoring them yields an early, calibrated infeasibility alarm that output-side confidence signals (perplexity, constraint-satisfaction probability) fail to provide.",
"Related Work": "SAE interpretability of scientific models (InterPLM 2024; ProtSAE 2025; Steering PLMs/ASPO 2025; the antibody SAE 2025; ProtoMech 2026; Matryoshka SAEs on ESM2-3B 2025) discovers and steers features toward SATISFIABLE single or multiple properties, always assuming a valid target exists, and evaluates whether the property appears. Hallucination-detection SAE work in text/vision LMs (SSL 2025; 'Do I Know This Entity?' 2024) shows features can flag when a model lacks knowledge, but concerns fuzzy factuality, not physically-verifiable constraint infeasibility. Constraint-based design/steering (compositional steering; conditioned generation) presumes feasibility and reports average satisfaction, never asking what happens when the requested constraint set is CONTRADICTORY. No prior work (a) constructs graded feasible-vs-infeasible design specs for proteins/molecules with objective, physics-based feasibility labels, (b) shows models silently and confidently violate constraints under infeasible specs, or (c) identifies interpretable 'frustration/infeasibility' features that fire selectively and act as a calibrated early alarm. This reframes interpretability from a controllability tool into an epistemic-honesty/safety instrument for design, distinct from all my prior steering-focused proposals and from hallucination work in non-scientific domains.",
"Abstract": "Scientific generative models are increasingly asked to satisfy multiple design constraints at once, but some constraint combinations are physically infeasible\u2014no valid protein or molecule can meet them (e.g., a compact fold with extreme surface-exposed hydrophobicity, or a small-molecule target combining mutually exclusive substructure and property demands). We surface a safety-relevant behavioral phenomenon: rather than refusing, models confidently generate a fluent, plausible-looking object that silently violates one constraint, and standard output-side confidence signals do not flag this. We then ask whether the model internally represents the infeasibility. Using ESM-2 protein language models and a SMILES chemical language model with sparse autoencoders (SAEs), we build graded feasibility ladders\u2014specs ranging from clearly satisfiable to provably infeasible\u2014with objective feasibility labels derived from physics/enumeration (e.g., co-occurrence bounds in natural data, RDKit/SMARTS satisfiability, structure-property incompatibility checks). We first quantify the silent-violation behavior and show output-side confidence is uninformative. We then search for interpretable 'frustration' features whose activation during constrained generation rises specifically as specs become infeasible, verify they are causal (ablation/steering shifts violation behavior and constraint-conflict resolution) and interpretable (they fire on the conflicting structural elements), and evaluate them as an early, calibrated infeasibility alarm versus perplexity and constraint-probability baselines. Success would give practitioners a cheap internal test that a requested design is impossible\u2014before expensive synthesis or validation\u2014and recast interpretable features as an epistemic-honesty instrument for scientific design.",
"Experiments": "1) MODELS, ORACLES, SAEs: Use ESM-2 (150M/650M) and a GPT-style SMILES chemical LM. Train TopK SAEs on the residual stream at a mid layer (intrinsic-dimension heuristic); verify reconstruction. Constraints have hard automated evaluators: proteins\u2014secondary-structure content (DSSP on ESMFold), GRAVY hydrophobicity, net charge, molecular weight, motif presence (HMMER/regex); molecules\u2014RDKit logP, QED, ring/aromatic counts, functional-group SMARTS, molecular weight. Validity gates: ESMFold pLDDT + pseudo-perplexity for proteins; RDKit-validity + SA for molecules.\n2) BUILD FEASIBILITY LADDERS (objective labels): For pairs/triples of constraints, construct a graded ladder from clearly feasible to provably infeasible. Feasibility labels come from signals independent of the generative model: (a) empirical co-occurrence bounds\u2014ranges of joint constraint values observed across a large natural corpus (a spec outside the empirical joint support is candidate-infeasible), (b) enumeration/SAT-style checks where possible\u2014e.g., SMARTS-based constraint conflicts that cannot co-exist in a valid molecule; incompatible protein constraints (e.g., >80% beta-sheet AND high solvent-exposed hydrophobicity) flagged via structure-property incompatibility rules, and (c) an oracle-search control: run a strong non-model optimizer (genetic search over sequences/molecules) to attempt to satisfy the spec; persistent failure across large budget corroborates infeasibility. Report the ladder and label confidence.\n3) SILENT-VIOLATION BEHAVIOR (core phenomenon): Condition/steer generation toward each spec (via feature or difference-of-means constraint steering) and measure, on FINISHED objects, per-constraint satisfaction and overall validity as feasibility decreases. Quantify: (a) silent-violation rate = fraction of infeasible-spec generations that remain valid/fluent but violate exactly one constraint (vs refusing/degenerating), (b) WHICH constraint the model sacrifices and whether this is systematic. Show output-side confidence is uninformative: correlate pseudo-perplexity, generation likelihood, and a constraint-satisfaction probe's confidence with true feasibility\u2014hypothesis: near-zero discrimination.\n4) FIND FRUSTRATION FEATURES (Location + Unit Interpretation): For each constraint pair, at multiple generation-progress fractions, compute each SAE feature's discrimination (AUROC / mutual information) of infeasible-vs-feasible specs, controlling for the constraint identity (so features detect CONFLICT, not just one property). Select a compact frustration-feature set. Auto-label them (max-activating contexts; LLM/annotation descriptions) and test whether they fire on the physically conflicting structural elements (e.g., the residues/atoms where the two demands collide).\n5) CAUSALITY (Causal Intervention): Ablate the frustration features and test whether the model's conflict-resolution changes (e.g., which constraint gets sacrificed shifts, or violation magnitude changes); amplify them and test whether generation is pushed toward hedging/lower-confidence completions. Use random-direction and matched-property-feature controls to establish specificity.\n6) EARLY INFEASIBILITY ALARM (application): Deploy the frustration-feature score as an early alarm that a spec is infeasible, read off partway through generation. Evaluate forecast AUROC and calibration vs generation progress, against baselines: partial perplexity/likelihood, a constraint-satisfaction probe on the partial object, and a black-box raw-activation probe. Metric: earliest-progress-to-reliable-detection, calibration (ECE), and precision@k for flagging infeasible specs. Practical payoff: compute saved by aborting/flagging infeasible design requests before full generation + ESMFold/synthesis-proxy validation.\n7) GENERALIZATION & ROBUSTNESS: Repeat across both domains, two model sizes, two SAE variants (TopK, Matryoshka); test whether frustration features transfer across constraint pairs (do the same features fire for different conflicts, indicating a general 'infeasibility' representation, or are they conflict-specific?). Report where the alarm fails (subtle infeasibilities).\nEVALUATION METRICS: silent-violation rate and sacrificed-constraint systematicity; discrimination of output-side confidence vs feasibility (should be near chance); frustration-feature AUROC/MI for infeasibility; causal specificity of ablation/amplification; early-alarm AUROC + calibration (ECE) + earliest-detection progress vs baselines; compute saved; cross-constraint transfer of frustration features.",
"Risk Factors and Limitations": "1) Feasibility labels are the crux and are imperfect: empirical co-occurrence support, SMARTS/structure incompatibility rules, and oracle-search failure are all in-silico proxies for true physical infeasibility. We mitigate by triangulating three independent signals and restricting core claims to specs where all three agree, and by reporting label-confidence-stratified results. 2) 'Infeasible' vs merely 'rare/hard' is a continuum; the oracle-search control and graded ladder are designed to separate genuinely impossible from hard-but-possible, but boundary cases will be noisy\u2014reported explicitly. 3) In-silico validity/property evaluators (ESMFold, RDKit) are proxies for wet-lab truth; claims concern model-internal epistemic signals, not experimental viability. 4) Frustration features might merely track the individual conflicting properties rather than their conflict; the constraint-identity control in feature selection and the causal conflict-resolution test are designed to rule this out. 5) The internal alarm may not beat a black-box raw-activation probe on raw AUROC; even so, interpretability (localizing the conflict), calibration, and early detection are the contribution and are reported honestly. 6) If models turn out to reliably signal infeasibility via output confidence, that is still a valuable positive result about epistemic honesty in scientific generative models. 7) SAE quality/layer choice could confound; controlled via multiple SAE variants, layers, and difference-of-means baselines."
}}
