Arguments: {"idea": {
  "Name": "provenance_shortcut_steering",
  "Title": "Designing the Database, Not the Molecule: Do Interpretable Features Reveal That Steered Scientific Generators Chase Dataset Provenance Instead of Physics?",
  "Short Hypothesis": "When we steer a protein/molecule generative model toward a desired PHYSICAL property (e.g., high thermostability), the model frequently satisfies the target by moving along interpretable features that encode DATASET PROVENANCE (source organism, protein family, structural-database membership, assay batch) rather than the underlying physics. The apparent property gain is a shortcut: it reproduces the provenance signature correlated with the property in the training data, and interpretable features expose this so we can detect it and steer against it.",
  "Related Work": "Prior pLM-SAE work (InterPLM 2024; ProtSAE 2025; 'From Mechanistic Interpretability to Mechanistic Biology' 2025; functional-annotation SAE work 2025) repeatedly finds that pLMs represent proteins via a mix of generic biophysical features AND strong 'family-specific'/organism-specific features, and steering studies add a target property by moving along whatever feature correlates with it. Separately, data-leakage and batch-effect work ('Beware of Data Leakage from Protein LLM Pretraining' 2024; thermostability leakage; batch-effect correction literature) shows downstream property predictors are inflated by provenance confounds. Recent critical work ('Dead Salmons of AI Interpretability' 2025; 'Automated Interpretability Metrics Do Not Distinguish Trained and Random Transformers' 2025; single-cell FM interpretability 2026 finding attention captures co-expression not causal signal) warns that interpretable-looking signals may be spurious. NO prior work connects these: no one asks whether interpretable-feature STEERING for design achieves property gains by exploiting provenance-artifact features rather than causal physics, quantifies how often this happens, or uses interpretability to disentangle a provenance-shortcut direction from a physics direction. This is distinct from all my prior proposals (compositionality, off-mode reach, steerability prediction, leakage, reliability collapse), which all assumed the property gain, when achieved, is legitimate.",
  "Abstract": "Steering interpretable features has become the standard way to make protein and molecule generators produce objects with a desired physical property, and success is judged by a property predictor. We surface a hidden behavioral phenomenon: because training corpora are riddled with provenance confounds (a property co-occurs with a source organism, a protein family, or a structural-database subset), a generator can satisfy a physical-property target by shifting the DATASET PROVENANCE of its output rather than its physics\u2014a shortcut that inflates the predictor but need not reflect real physical mechanism. We use interpretability to expose this. Training sparse autoencoders on ESM-2 (proteins) and a SMILES chemical LM, we identify two kinds of feature directions per target property: physics-aligned directions (correlated with the property after controlling for provenance) and provenance-aligned directions (correlated with source organism/family/database membership). We test three claims: (1) standard property-steering moves substantially along provenance features, and its gain shrinks or vanishes when scored by a provenance-controlled oracle; (2) the fraction of the achieved property gain attributable to provenance predicts a designer-relevant failure\u2014steered designs cluster tightly with a training-data provenance group and lose novelty/mechanistic diversity; and (3) explicitly orthogonalizing the steering direction against provenance features (provenance-invariant steering) preserves genuine property gain while restoring novelty and provenance-controlled predictor agreement. We report a provenance-shortcut score, its correlation with spurious gains, and a simple debiasing recipe. Results recast interpretable features as an audit that separates designing-the-molecule from designing-the-database.",
  "Experiments": "1) MODELS, PROVENANCE LABELS, ORACLES: Use ESM-2 (150M/650M) and a GPT-style SMILES chemical LM. Train TopK SAEs on the residual stream at a mid layer (intrinsic-dimension heuristic); verify reconstruction. Target PHYSICAL properties with cheap evaluators: proteins\u2014thermostability proxy (fine-tuned head), GRAVY, secondary-structure content (DSSP on ESMFold); molecules\u2014logP, solubility proxy, QED. PROVENANCE labels available per training object: proteins\u2014source organism/taxon, Pfam family, and structural-database (PDB/CATH) membership; molecules\u2014source assay/dataset (ChEMBL target/document id), scaffold class. These are the confounds documented by the data-leakage literature.\n2) IDENTIFY PHYSICS VS PROVENANCE FEATURES: For each SAE feature, compute (a) its correlation with the target property and (b) its correlation with provenance labels across held-out natural objects. Partition features into provenance-aligned (high provenance MI), physics-aligned (property correlation surviving provenance stratification / partial correlation), and mixed. Report how entangled property and provenance are in feature space per domain.\n3) CLAIM 1\u2014STANDARD STEERING RIDES PROVENANCE: Apply standard property steering (best-property-correlated SAE feature and difference-of-means direction) at a swept budget; generate objects. Measure (i) property gain by the naive predictor, and (ii) property gain by a PROVENANCE-CONTROLLED oracle\u2014either a predictor trained on a provenance-balanced/decorrelated split, or an independent physics evaluator (FoldX/Rosetta-style stability; a second empirical logP model) that does not use provenance. Decompose the steering direction's projection onto provenance vs physics feature subspaces. Primary metric: fraction of steering displacement in the provenance subspace, and the naive-minus-controlled property-gain gap (the 'spurious gain'). Include random-direction controls.\n4) CLAIM 2\u2014SHORTCUT PREDICTS DESIGNER-RELEVANT FAILURE: For each steered generation, compute a provenance-shortcut score (share of gain attributable to provenance movement) and measure downstream consequences: provenance clustering (does the design collapse toward one organism/family/scaffold group in embedding space?), novelty (identity/Tanimoto to nearest training object), and mechanistic diversity of the set. Regress these on the shortcut score (Spearman/R^2). Hypothesis: high-shortcut steering yields provenance-collapsed, low-novelty designs whose 'property' does not survive the controlled oracle.\n5) CLAIM 3\u2014PROVENANCE-INVARIANT STEERING (fix): Construct a debiased steering direction by orthogonalizing the property direction against the provenance feature subspace (Gram-Schmidt / projection removal). Compare provenance-invariant steering vs standard steering on the control-property-gain, provenance-collapse, novelty, and validity axes at matched displacement. Hypothesis: invariant steering preserves controlled property gain while restoring novelty and reducing provenance collapse; quantify any loss in raw naive-predictor gain (which was partly spurious).\n6) POSITIVE CONTROL: Inject a synthetic provenance confound (relabel a subset so a property artificially co-occurs with a tag) into a probe/predictor setup and confirm the pipeline recovers the planted shortcut and the fix removes it.\n7) ROBUSTNESS: Repeat across both domains, two model sizes, two SAE variants (TopK, Matryoshka), and multiple properties; report which properties are most provenance-confounded and where the effect is stable vs artifact.\nEVALUATION METRICS: provenance-subspace displacement fraction; naive-vs-controlled property-gain gap (spurious gain, primary); shortcut-score vs provenance-collapse/novelty Spearman/R^2; provenance-invariant-steering deltas on controlled gain, novelty, collapse, validity; positive-control recovery; per-property confound ranking.",
  "Risk Factors and Limitations": "1) Provenance-controlled oracles and physics evaluators (FoldX/Rosetta, second logP model) are in-silico proxies; the core claim rests on DISAGREEMENT between a naive predictor and a provenance-decorrelated one, plus displacement into a provenance feature subspace\u2014stated explicitly, not as wet-lab truth. 2) Physics and provenance may be irreducibly entangled for some properties (family IS the mechanism); we handle this by reporting the entanglement per property and restricting strong claims to properties where a provenance-orthogonal physics direction demonstrably exists (validated by the controlled oracle). 3) The debiasing fix could remove genuine signal if physics and provenance share a subspace; we quantify the tradeoff via the controlled oracle rather than assume a free lunch. 4) SAE quality/layer choice could produce spurious 'provenance features'; controlled with multiple SAE variants, difference-of-means baselines, random-direction controls, and the synthetic positive control (experiment 6). 5) If standard steering turns out NOT to ride provenance (gains survive the controlled oracle), that is a valuable positive result establishing that interpretable-feature steering targets physics, not database artifacts. 6) In-silico property/validity metrics limit conclusions to model-internal design behavior, not experimental function."
}}
