Arguments: {"idea": {"Name": "symmetry_shortcut_crystal", "Title": "Symmetry Without Understanding? Auditing Whether Crystal Generative Models Causally Represent Space-Group Constraints or Silently Fake Them", "Short Hypothesis": "Crystal generative models conditioned on a target space group satisfy the constraint not because they possess a compact, causally-manipulable internal representation of the requested symmetry, but via a shallow lattice/Wyckoff-copying shortcut. We hypothesize (i) there is a decodable but only weakly causally-steerable internal 'space-group' direction; (ii) steering it to request a NEW space group frequently yields structures whose achieved symmetry silently mismatches the request (wrong space group, lower symmetry, or broken periodicity) while still passing validity/stability checks; and (iii) an intervention-free internal symmetry-consistency signal predicts these silent failures better than output-side likelihood or formation-energy proxies.", "Related Work": "Symmetry-aware crystal generation is a rich area: SymmCD (2025), DiffCSP++/Space-Group-Constrained Generation (2024), WyCryst (2023), and PGCGM (2022) either hard-code space-group/Wyckoff constraints or condition on them. Critically, Ishii et al. (2026, WyckoffDiff-Adaptor) show that conditional symmetry control 'may not be sufficiently effective when space group constraints are applied as a condition'\u2014i.e., models silently violate the requested symmetry\u2014but treat this as an architecture problem, not a representational one. Interpretability in materials (CGCNN 2018, Site-Net 2022, RankAAE 2023) is confined to PREDICTIVE property models with attention/latent-descriptor analysis; none examines the internal mechanism of GENERATIVE crystal models, and none asks whether symmetry\u2014the defining, physics-critical property of crystals\u2014is a genuine causal handle or a copying shortcut. No prior work (a) locates and causally tests a space-group representation inside a crystal generator, (b) shows symmetry-conditioned generation silently fakes the requested symmetry via a shortcut, or (c) provides an internal symmetry-reliability audit that catches these failures. This distinguishes the proposal from all symmetry-architecture work (which changes the model) and mirrors, in a new object class and for a new property (crystallographic symmetry vs stereochemistry), the shortcut-auditing lens of prior molecular proposals.", "Abstract": "Symmetry is the defining property of a crystal: its space group dictates physical behavior and is the primary control knob in modern crystal generative models, which either hard-code it or condition on it. Yet recent evidence shows conditional symmetry control can silently fail\u2014models emit structures that do not have the requested space group. We ask a mechanistic question no prior work addresses: do crystal generators actually possess an internal, causally-manipulable representation of the requested symmetry, or do they satisfy the constraint through a shallow lattice/Wyckoff-copying shortcut that mimics symmetry without understanding it? Using open symmetry-conditioned diffusion generators (e.g., DiffCSP++/SymmCD-style models) trained on Materials Project data, we (1) LOCATE candidate space-group representations by probing the denoiser's internal activations for the target space group and lattice class; (2) CAUSALLY test whether a compact intervention can convert generation from one space group to another\u2014producing a structure whose ACHIEVED symmetry (verified by pymatgen SpacegroupAnalyzer at tolerance sweeps) matches the new request while composition and validity are preserved\u2014the operational definition of a genuine symmetry handle; (3) INTERPRET whether the located units encode true symmetry (invariant to equivalent lattice re-descriptions and origin choices) or shallow lattice-parameter/Wyckoff-token statistics; and (4) AUDIT symmetry-conditioned design reliability, measuring the SILENT SYMMETRY-ERROR RATE\u2014requested-vs-achieved space-group mismatches that pass validity/stability screens\u2014and whether an intervention-free internal symmetry-consistency score flags them better than likelihood or formation-energy proxies. Results would recast a headline capability of crystal generators as a potentially unreliable shortcut and deliver a cheap pre-flight symmetry-trust filter for materials design.", "Experiments": "1) MODELS, DATA, ORACLES: Use open symmetry-conditioned crystal diffusion generators with accessible per-step denoiser activations (DiffCSP++ / SymmCD / WyckoffDiff-style checkpoints) trained on Materials Project or MP-20. Ground-truth symmetry via pymatgen SpacegroupAnalyzer with a tolerance sweep (record achieved space group, crystal system, point group, Wyckoff multiplicities). Validity gates: physical plausibility (bond-length/overlap checks, charge neutrality, StructureMatcher-based novelty) and stability proxy (energy-above-hull via a pretrained universal ML interatomic potential such as CHGNet/MACE-MP; NO DFT needed). First establish a BASELINE that, unconditionally, the model reproduces target space groups above chance so absence claims are meaningful.\n2) LOCATION\u2014is space group decodable? Train linear/MLP probes on the denoiser residual-stream activations (at multiple denoising timesteps and layers) to predict the conditioned target space group, crystal system, and lattice class. Report probe accuracy vs timestep/layer; identify top candidate 'space-group' features/directions. Control probe: predict a purely surface-level quantity (e.g., the raw conditioning-token embedding) to gauge how much decoding is trivial copy of the condition input.\n3) CAUSAL INTERVENTION\u2014is there a space-group SWITCH handle? (core test) Take generations conditioned on space group A; intervene on the located feature/direction (clamp/steer, and activation-patch from a run conditioned on space group B) and complete denoising. Measure SYMMETRY-SWITCH SUCCESS RATE = fraction of interventions producing a finished structure whose SpacegroupAnalyzer-verified symmetry equals B, while (a) composition is preserved, (b) validity/stability retained, and (c) the change is specific (random-direction and matched-non-symmetry-feature controls do nothing). A genuine handle yields high, specific switching; a shortcut yields symmetry breaking, reversion to A, collapse to a lower-symmetry subgroup, or invalid structures. Compare probe-derived directions, difference-of-means (B-minus-A) directions, and full activation patching; report sign, dose-response, and subgroup/supergroup relationships of failures.\n4) UNIT INTERPRETATION\u2014true symmetry or lattice-statistics shortcut? Construct controlled crystal pairs that dissociate space group from surface descriptors: (i) same space group with different lattice parameters / origin choice / equivalent unit-cell settings; (ii) different space groups with similar lattice parameters. Test whether the located feature tracks the true space group (invariant to equivalent re-descriptions) or the lattice-parameter/Wyckoff-token statistics. A feature that changes meaning under a symmetry-preserving cell re-description is a shortcut, not a symmetry concept.\n5) DECISION AUDITING\u2014symmetry-conditioned design reliability (payoff): Across the full space-group vocabulary (stratified by crystal system and symmetry order), request each space group and measure the SILENT SYMMETRY-ERROR RATE = fraction of VALID+stable outputs whose achieved space group differs from the requested one (broken down into: correct crystal system but wrong space group, dropped to a subgroup, or fully broken symmetry), stratified by requested symmetry order and how common the space group is in training data (linking failure to data frequency). Critically, test whether output-side signals (generation likelihood, formation-energy/e-above-hull proxy, validity checks) detect these mismatches\u2014hypothesis: near-chance\u2014while the INTERNAL symmetry-consistency score (probe confidence / feature coherence read off mid-generation) flags them, yielding a pre-flight symmetry-trust filter. Report AUROC and calibration (ECE) of internal vs output-side detectors, and compute saved by aborting/flagging untrustworthy requests before full generation + relaxation.\n6) ROBUSTNESS: Repeat across two generator architectures (a coordinate-based diffusion and a Wyckoff-based diffusion), two SpacegroupAnalyzer tolerances, and high- vs low-symmetry space groups; test whether switch success/failure and silent-error rate track training-set space-group frequency and symmetry order.\nEVALUATION METRICS: probe accuracy for space group/system (Location); SYMMETRY-SWITCH SUCCESS RATE and specificity (primary causal metric); feature-meaning invariance under equivalent cell re-descriptions (interpretation); SILENT SYMMETRY-ERROR RATE and internal-vs-output-side detection AUROC/calibration (auditing); dependence on symmetry order and training frequency.", "Risk Factors and Limitations": "1) The core claim is partly an ABSENCE claim (no clean causal symmetry handle); we mitigate by trying multiple intervention types (probe direction, difference-of-means, full activation patching), sweeping strength, and requiring the step-1 baseline to confirm the model does reproduce target space groups\u2014so a null switch result is meaningful, not a weak-model artifact. A positive result (a genuine steerable symmetry handle) is equally publishable and useful for symmetry-controlled design. 2) Achieved-symmetry ground truth depends on SpacegroupAnalyzer tolerance; we sweep tolerances and report sensitivity, restricting strong claims to tolerance-robust cases. 3) Stability is assessed by ML interatomic potentials (CHGNet/MACE), an in-silico proxy for DFT/synthesizability; claims concern requested-vs-achieved symmetry (an objective crystallographic fact) and model-internal representation, not experimental synthesizability. 4) Requires generators with accessible per-step activations; scope limited to open, instrumentable models. 5) An internal probe might not beat a black-box raw-activation probe on raw AUROC; even so, the interpretability diagnosis (shortcut vs concept) and the reliability-audit payoff are the contributions and are reported honestly. 6) Symmetry and lattice statistics may be irreducibly entangled for some space groups; the controlled re-description pairs (step 4) are designed to separate them and we report where separation is impossible."}}
