Arguments: {"idea": {"Name": "rna_folding_mirage_steering", "Title": "The Folding Mirage: Do Interpretable Features Control an RNA's Local Motifs While Silently Breaking Its Global Thermodynamic Fold?", "Short Hypothesis": "Interpretable sparse-autoencoder features of RNA language models afford causal, steerable control over LOCAL structural motifs (a hairpin, a stem, a poly-U tract), but NOT over the GLOBAL thermodynamic fold that defines RNA function. Consequently, steering a feature to insert a desired local structure silently produces sequences whose true minimum-free-energy fold and target-structure Boltzmann probability collapse\u2014a 'folding mirage'\u2014that motif-content and validity checks miss, but which an intervention-free internal thermodynamic-consistency signal flags.", "Related Work": "RNA language model interpretability is nascent and purely descriptive: SAE-RNA (2025), SPIRAL/BiRNA-BERT (2026), and small gene-LM SAE work (2025) all find SAE features that localize to stems, hairpins, poly-G/C/A/U tracts and ncRNA families, but none steers generation or asks whether steering preserves the global fold. RNA design LMs (RNAinformer 2024; 'Designing RNAs with Language Models' 2026; AIDO.RNA inverse folding 2025) do supervised/RL inverse folding to hit a target secondary structure but offer no interpretability, no feature-level steering, and no audit of when control silently fails. Protein/molecule steering-audit work (InterPLM, ProtSAE, and my prior chirality/symmetry/syntax proposals) establishes the content-vs-global-property axis in other object classes but never in RNA. RNA is uniquely suited to this question because its defining functional property\u2014the global fold\u2014has an exact, instant, physics-grounded oracle (ViennaRNA MFE, partition function, and Boltzmann probability of any target structure), turning 'silent global failure' from a proxy into an objectively computable quantity. No prior work (a) causally steers RNA-LM features, (b) contrasts local-motif steerability against global-fold steerability, or (c) surfaces and audits the folding-mirage phenomenon. This is the first interpretability-of-generation study for RNA and the first to exploit RNA thermodynamics as a clean ground-truth oracle for steering reliability.", "Abstract": "An RNA molecule's function is determined by its global thermodynamic fold, not merely by which local motifs it contains: the same hairpin can be part of a functional structure or buried in a completely different minimum-free-energy conformation. Interpretability-guided sequence design increasingly steers language-model features to add desired structural elements, judged by whether the motif appears. We surface a behavioral phenomenon we call the folding mirage: steering an interpretable feature to insert a local structure (a hairpin, a stem) reliably increases that local motif's presence but drives the sequence's true global fold\u2014its minimum-free-energy structure and the Boltzmann probability of the intended target\u2014to collapse, a failure invisible to motif-content and validity checks. We then ask a mechanistic question: do RNA language models represent the global fold as a compact, causally-steerable feature the way they represent local motifs, or is global thermodynamic consistency emergent and non-steerable? RNA is the ideal testbed because ViennaRNA computes the exact global fold, ensemble free energy, and target-structure Boltzmann probability instantly and for free. Using RiNALMo/RNA-FM with sparse autoencoders, we (1) LOCATE candidate local-motif and global-fold features via probing; (2) CAUSALLY test the steerability of each, contrasting local-motif control against global-fold control; (3) quantify the mirage\u2014the drop in target-structure Boltzmann probability that local-motif steering incurs; and (4) AUDIT reliability, testing whether an internal thermodynamic-consistency signal flags mirage sequences better than motif-content or model likelihood. We predict local control succeeds, global control is decodable-but-weakly-steerable, and a cheap internal audit catches silently misfolded designs.", "Experiments": "1) MODELS, SAEs, ORACLES: Use public RNA language models RiNALMo (650M) and RNA-FM with TopK (and Ordered, for steerability, following the antibody-SAE finding) SAEs trained on the residual stream at a layer chosen by an intrinsic-dimension heuristic; verify reconstruction fidelity. THERMODYNAMIC oracle (cheap, exact): ViennaRNA\u2014RNAfold for the MFE structure and free energy; the partition function for ensemble free energy; and the Boltzmann probability that a sequence folds into any specified TARGET structure (the primary global-fold signal). LOCAL-MOTIF oracle: presence/position of specified secondary-structure elements (a hairpin loop of given length, a stem of given length, a bulge) extracted from the predicted structure, plus sequence tracts (poly-U/G/C). Validity gates: composition sanity (GC content bounds, no degenerate runs), RNA-LM pseudo-perplexity.\n2) FEATURE BANK & LOCATION: Identify interpretable features via concept-correlation/probe AUROC on held-out ncRNA sequences: (a) LOCAL-MOTIF features (fire on a specific hairpin/stem/tract, per SAE-RNA/SPIRAL findings), and (b) candidate GLOBAL-FOLD features (correlate with global properties\u2014MFE per nucleotide, ensemble free energy, overall base-pairing fraction, or membership in a global fold class\u2014controlling for local motif content). Report probe AUROC/R^2 for local vs global; identify top candidate directions; compare against a raw-activation probe; test whether global-fold information is decodable at all.\n3) CORE PHENOMENON\u2014THE FOLDING MIRAGE (local-easy/global-hard): For each local-motif feature, sweep steering strength and generate/infill N sequences per level (masked infilling for encoder models). At each level measure (i) local-motif gain (does the target hairpin/stem appear in the predicted structure?), (ii) GLOBAL-fold health\u2014Boltzmann probability of the intended overall target structure and MFE-structure agreement with intent, and (iii) validity. Quantify the mirage = drop in target-structure Boltzmann probability per unit local-motif gain, its dose-response, and the SILENT-MISFOLD RATE = fraction of local-motif-satisfying, composition-valid sequences whose global fold is thermodynamically wrong. Show the blind spot: correlate local-motif satisfaction and pseudo-perplexity with true global-fold health (hypothesis: near-zero\u2014standard checks miss the mirage). Random-direction and matched-non-motif-feature controls.\n4) CAUSAL GLOBAL-FOLD TEST: Steer candidate global-fold features and activation-patch from sequences with correct global folds; test whether we can improve the target-structure Boltzmann probability / shift the global fold class while HOLDING local motif content fixed\u2014the operational definition of a global-fold handle. Compare SAE-feature steering, difference-of-means (well-folded-vs-misfolded) directions, and activation patching; report sign, dose-response, and specificity. Head-to-head calibrate against local-motif steerability in the same pipeline. Hypothesis: global fold is decodable but far less steerable than local motifs (Ordered SAEs may recover partial steerability\u2014test this).\n5) INTERPRETATION: Test whether located global-fold units encode true thermodynamic fold (invariant to local-motif identity, tracking MFE/ensemble energy) vs shallow local composition, using controlled sequence pairs that dissociate global fold from local content (same hairpin embedded in well-folded vs misfolded global contexts).\n6) DECISION AUDITING (payoff): Deploy an intervention-free internal THERMODYNAMIC-CONSISTENCY score (global-fold probe confidence / feature coherence read mid-generation). Measure whether it flags mirage sequences (local-OK, global-broken) better than output-side signals (motif content, pseudo-perplexity, model likelihood): report AUROC/ECE of internal vs output-side detectors, and compute saved by flagging misfolded designs before expensive downstream 3D/functional prediction. Emit human-readable diagnoses ('hairpin present but sequestered in an alternative MFE fold, target Boltzmann prob 0.02').\n7) ROBUSTNESS: Repeat across RiNALMo vs RNA-FM, short (tRNA-scale) vs longer ncRNA, TopK vs Ordered SAEs, and two SAE layers; report where the mirage and (non-)steerability findings are stable vs artifact, and whether the mirage tracks how far off-distribution the requested motif combination pushes generation.\nEVALUATION METRICS: folding-mirage magnitude & dose-response and SILENT-MISFOLD RATE (primary phenomenon, via ViennaRNA target-structure Boltzmann probability); local-check-vs-global-fold correlation (blind spot); local vs global probe AUROC/R^2 (Location); global-fold-steering success/specificity vs local-motif-steering (Causal Intervention); global-fold-feature invariance to local content (Interpretation); internal-vs-output-side detection AUROC/ECE and screening saved (auditing); robustness across models/lengths/SAEs.", "Risk Factors and Limitations": "1) Global fold is assessed by ViennaRNA (nearest-neighbor thermodynamic model), which is a well-validated but still in-silico oracle for secondary structure; it ignores tertiary interactions/pseudoknots and cellular context, so claims concern thermodynamic-model-verified global folding, not wet-lab function\u2014stated explicitly. We can corroborate a subset with a structure-aware model (ERNIE-RNA/structRFM) and report agreement. 2) The global-fold-non-steerability claim is partly an ABSENCE claim; we mitigate by trying multiple intervention types (TopK and Ordered SAE features, difference-of-means, activation patching), sweeping strength, and head-to-head calibrating that LOCAL-motif features ARE steerable in the same pipeline\u2014so a null global result is meaningful, not a weak-model artifact. A positive result (a genuine steerable global-fold handle) is equally publishable and directly useful for structure-aware RNA design. 3) The mirage could be confounded with generic off-distribution drift; we use random-direction and matched-non-motif-feature controls and test whether the mirage tracks motif-specific displacement. 4) Local and global structure are partly entangled (a large motif dominates the fold); the controlled dissociation pairs (step 5) separate them and we report where separation is impossible. 5) SAE quality/layer choice could confound Location; controlled with TopK and Ordered SAEs, multiple layers, raw-activation probes, and random-direction controls. 6) An internal consistency probe might not beat a black-box raw-activation probe on raw AUROC; the interpretability diagnosis (local-decodable, global-weakly-steerable) and the audit payoff remain the contributions, reported honestly. 7) If no mirage is found (local steering preserves global folds), that is a valuable positive result establishing that RNA-LM feature steering is thermodynamically safe."}}
