Response Content: {"total": 1, "offset": 0, "data": [{"paperId": "8edaab0e929a43a3d585c366c68deb0e5dc87bb5", "title": "New formulae for relative magnetic helicity", "venue": "", "year": 2013, "citationCount": 0, "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at http://sun.bao.ac.cn/meetings/HT2013/HT2013-abstract.pdf, which is subject to the license by the author or copyrig
Action: FinalizeIdea
Arguments: {"idea": {"Name": "conservation_law_mirage_reactions", "Title": "Balanced by Habit, Not by Law: Do Reaction Generative Models Internally Represent Mass Conservation as a Steerable Feature, or Fake It?", "Short Hypothesis": "Autoregressive reaction-prediction models produce atom-balanced reactions (reactants and products with matching element counts) not because they possess a compact, causally-steerable internal representation of the conservation LAW, but via a shallow atom-copying heuristic tied to local token context. Consequently, steering an interpretable feature to alter a product's chemistry (add/remove an atom or functional group) silently breaks mass balance\u2014a 'conservation mirage'\u2014that ordinary SMILES-validity checks miss, while an intervention-free internal balance-consistency signal flags it. We further hypothesize there is no compact steerable 'atom-balance' feature the way there are steerable chemistry features, making conservation an unrecognized interpretability blind spot.", "Related Work": "FlowER (2025) and atom-conserving CRNNs (2023) show data-driven reaction models routinely VIOLATE mass/atom conservation, producing 'hallucinatory' unbalanced reactions, and fix this ARCHITECTURALLY by hard-coding electron/atom-balance layers\u2014treating conservation as an external constraint, never asking whether a standard model internally represents it. 'Circuits, Features, and Heuristics in Molecular Transformers' (2025) finds molecular transformers implement ring/branch SYNTAX circuits and a steerable valence-capacity direction, and 'Physics Steering' (2025) shows physics foundation models have steerable concept directions\u2014but neither studies reactions or the conservation invariant, and neither asks whether a global conservation law (as opposed to a local property) is a steerable handle. Conservation-law discovery work (Noether-from-DNN 2021; stoichiometry-nullspace methods 2014/2024) extracts laws from PREDICTIVE dynamics models, never from a generative reaction LM's internal features, and never tests steering reliability. No prior work (a) asks whether a generative reaction model represents mass/atom conservation as a causal, steerable feature, (b) surfaces the conservation-mirage phenomenon where chemistry-steering silently unbalances a reaction, or (c) provides an internal balance-reliability audit. This introduces the content-vs-conservation-law axis into interpretability-of-generation for chemical reactions\u2014a new object class where conservation is an exact, instantly computable oracle (element-count matching / stoichiometry null space)\u2014distinct from all prior single-property steering and from all architectural conservation fixes.", "Abstract": "Mass conservation is the most basic law of chemistry: a valid reaction has identical element counts on both sides. Yet data-driven reaction models are known to hallucinate unbalanced reactions, and the field fixes this by hard-coding balance into the architecture\u2014never asking whether a standard model actually understands conservation internally. We surface and explain a behavioral phenomenon we call the conservation mirage. Autoregressive reaction-prediction transformers produce mostly balanced reactions, but we hypothesize they do so via a shallow atom-copying heuristic rather than a genuine internal conservation law: steering an interpretable feature to change a product's chemistry (add a methyl, swap a halogen, remove an oxygen) reliably changes the chemistry but silently breaks atom balance, a failure invisible to SMILES-validity checks and evident only from element counting. We then ask a mechanistic question: is mass/atom conservation represented as a compact, causally-steerable feature\u2014the way local chemistry features demonstrably are\u2014or is it emergent and non-steerable? Reactions are the ideal testbed because conservation is an exact, free oracle: element-count vectors (and the stoichiometry null space) instantly certify balance. Using an autoregressive reaction transformer trained on USPTO reactions with sparse autoencoders, we (1) LOCATE candidate chemistry features and candidate conservation features via probing; (2) CAUSALLY test the steerability of each, contrasting local-chemistry control against atom-balance control; (3) quantify the mirage\u2014the balance-breakage that chemistry-steering incurs; and (4) AUDIT reliability, testing whether an internal balance-consistency signal flags unbalanced designs better than validity or model likelihood. We predict chemistry is steerable, conservation is decodable-but-weakly-steerable, and a cheap internal audit catches silently unbalanced reactions before wet-lab or DFT screening.", "Experiments": "1) MODEL, SAEs, ORACLES: Train (or use a public checkpoint of) an autoregressive reaction transformer on USPTO reaction SMILES (reactants>reagents>products), retaining atom-mapping where available. Train TopK (and Ordered/Matryoshka, for steerability, following the antibody-SAE finding that TopK features can be decodable-but-inert) SAEs on the residual stream at a mid layer chosen by an intrinsic-dimension heuristic; verify reconstruction. CONSERVATION oracle (exact, free via RDKit): element-count vector of reactants minus products; a reaction is atom-balanced iff the difference is zero (also compute charge balance and, where atom-mapping exists, per-atom mapping completeness). LOCAL-CHEMISTRY oracle (RDKit): presence/absence of specified product functional groups or atoms (SMARTS), product molecular formula deltas. Validity gates: RDKit-parseable, valence-valid SMILES on both sides, model pseudo-perplexity. First establish a BASELINE that the model natively produces balanced reactions well above chance, so absence claims are meaningful.\n2) FEATURE BANK & LOCATION: Identify interpretable features via concept-correlation/probe AUROC on held-out reactions: (a) LOCAL-CHEMISTRY features (fire when a product contains a given functional group / atom type), and (b) candidate CONSERVATION features (correlate with the reactant-minus-product element-count residual, or with 'is-balanced' status, controlling for reaction class). Report probe AUROC/R^2 for chemistry vs conservation; identify top candidate directions; compare against a raw-activation probe; test whether balance status is decodable at all and at which generation position (during product decoding).\n3) CORE PHENOMENON\u2014THE CONSERVATION MIRAGE (chemistry-easy/conservation-hard): For each chemistry feature, sweep steering strength and generate N product completions per level given fixed reactants. At each level measure (i) chemistry gain (did the intended group/atom change appear in the product?), (ii) BALANCE health (element-count residual = 0? magnitude of imbalance in atoms), and (iii) SMILES validity. Quantify the mirage = increase in atom imbalance per unit chemistry gain, its dose-response, and the SILENT-IMBALANCE RATE = fraction of chemistry-satisfying, SMILES-valid reactions that are mass-unbalanced. Show the blind spot: correlate SMILES-validity and pseudo-perplexity with true balance (hypothesis: near-zero\u2014standard checks miss imbalance). Random-direction and matched-non-chemistry-feature controls.\n4) CAUSAL CONSERVATION TEST: Steer candidate conservation features and activation-patch from balanced-reaction runs; test whether we can RESTORE atom balance (drive the element-count residual toward zero) while holding the intended product chemistry fixed\u2014the operational definition of a conservation handle. Compare SAE-feature steering, difference-of-means (balanced-vs-unbalanced) directions, and activation patching; report sign, dose-response, and specificity. Head-to-head calibrate against chemistry-feature steerability in the same pipeline. Hypothesis: conservation is decodable but far less steerable than chemistry (test whether Ordered SAEs recover partial steerability).\n5) UNIT INTERPRETATION: Test whether located conservation units encode a true global balance concept (invariant to reaction class / molecule identity, tracking the element-count residual) versus a shallow local atom-copying heuristic, using controlled reaction pairs that dissociate balance from local product content (same product functional group in balanced vs deliberately unbalanced reactions). Auto-label top features via max-activating contexts.\n6) DECISION AUDITING (payoff): Deploy an intervention-free internal BALANCE-CONSISTENCY score (conservation-probe confidence / feature coherence read mid-generation) as an early alarm. Measure whether it flags mirage reactions (chemistry-OK, mass-broken) better than output-side signals (SMILES-validity, pseudo-perplexity, model likelihood): report AUROC/ECE of internal vs output-side detectors, and compute saved by flagging unbalanced reactions before expensive downstream feasibility/DFT screening. Emit human-readable diagnoses ('product gains a CH3 but reactants provide no carbon source; imbalance +1 C +3 H').\n7) ROBUSTNESS: Repeat across two model sizes, TopK vs Ordered/Matryoshka SAEs, two SAE layers, and forward-prediction vs retrosynthesis framing; report where the mirage and (non-)steerability findings are stable vs artifact, and whether the mirage tracks how far off-distribution the requested chemistry change pushes the product.\nEVALUATION METRICS: conservation-mirage magnitude & dose-response and SILENT-IMBALANCE RATE (primary phenomenon, via exact RDKit element counting); validity-vs-balance correlation (blind spot); chemistry vs conservation probe AUROC/R^2 (Location); conservation-restoration steering success/specificity vs chemistry-steering (Causal Intervention); conservation-feature invariance to reaction class (Interpretation); internal-vs-output-side detection AUROC/ECE and screening saved (auditing); robustness across models/SAEs/framings.", "Risk Factors and Limitations": "1) Mass/atom balance is an EXACT, non-proxy oracle (element counting is deterministic), which is a strength; the main proxy is downstream 'feasibility', which we deliberately do not claim\u2014core claims concern the objectively-computable conservation invariant, not reaction viability. 2) The conservation-non-steerability claim is partly an ABSENCE claim; we mitigate by trying multiple intervention types (TopK and Ordered SAE features, difference-of-means, activation patching), sweeping strength, and head-to-head calibrating that CHEMISTRY features ARE steerable in the same pipeline\u2014so a null conservation result is meaningful rather than a weak-model artifact. A positive result (a genuine steerable conservation handle) is equally publishable and directly useful for building balance-aware reaction models without architectural surgery. 3) The mirage could be confounded with generic off-distribution drift; we use random-direction and matched-non-chemistry-feature controls and test whether the mirage tracks chemistry-specific displacement. 4) Chemistry and balance are partly entangled (a chemistry edit that adds an atom must be sourced from a reactant); the controlled dissociation pairs (step 5) and the atom-source diagnostics are designed to separate 'model knows the atom must come from somewhere' from 'model copies atoms locally', and we report where separation is impossible. 5) Some USPTO reactions are themselves unbalanced/incompletely recorded; we filter to a curated balanced-reaction training/eval subset and report label quality. 6) SAE quality/layer choice could confound Location; controlled with TopK and Ordered SAEs, multiple layers, raw-activation probes, and random-direction controls. 7) An internal balance probe might not beat a black-box raw-activation probe on raw AUROC; the interpretability diagnosis (chemistry-decodable, conservation-weakly-steerable, heuristic-vs-law) and the audit payoff remain the contributions, reported honestly. 8) If no mirage is found (chemistry steering preserves balance), that is a valuable positive result establishing that reaction-model feature steering is conservation-safe and that the model represents conservation robustly."}}
