Arguments: {"idea": {"Name": "physics_field_conservation_steering", "Title": "Steer the Storm, Break the Balance: Do Interpretable Interventions on Physics-Field Emulators Silently Violate Conservation Laws?", "Short Hypothesis": "Data-driven physics-field emulators (weather models, fluid/PDE surrogates) possess interpretable, causally-steerable features for LOCAL/phenomenological structures (a cyclone, a vortex, a diffusion front), but do NOT possess a compact, causally-steerable representation of the GLOBAL CONSERVATION LAWS (mass, energy, momentum) that certify a field as physical. Consequently, steering a feature to modify a local phenomenon\u2014the exact intervention celebrated in recent physics-steering work\u2014silently breaks the conserved global integrals, a 'conservation blind spot' that local plausibility and per-cell validity checks miss but an exact conservation-integral oracle exposes; and an intervention-free internal conservation-consistency signal flags it.", "Related Work": "Physics Steering (2025) shows a physics foundation model has single directions causally steering vorticity, diffusion, and simulation speed; the GraphCast SAE paper (2025) finds interpretable features (cyclones, atmospheric rivers, sea-ice) and shows sparse feature modifications yield 'physically consistent' evolving hurricanes; CFD-surrogate SAE work (2025) extracts monosemantic vorticity/flow features; DIANO and flow-matching-interpretability work embed physics into latent spaces. Crucially, EVERY one of these steers or interprets LOCAL, phenomenological structures and asserts the change 'looks physically consistent' by eyeball or per-region metrics\u2014NONE verifies that the intervention preserves the GLOBAL conserved integrals (total mass/energy/momentum, or the discrete divergence/continuity constraint) that actually define physical validity. Separately, conservation-aware ML (physics-informed losses, hard-constraint layers, FlowER for reaction mass balance) treats conservation as an architectural constraint, never asking whether a standard emulator internally represents it or whether interpretable steering respects it. No prior work (a) tests conservation-law preservation of interpretable-feature interventions on physics-field generators, (b) contrasts local-phenomenon steerability against conservation-law steerability, or (c) provides an internal conservation-consistency audit. This is distinct from all my prior discrete-object proposals (including chemical-reaction atom balance, which counts atoms in a string) because here conservation is a CONTINUOUS field integral / differential constraint over a spatial grid, and the object class (weather/PDE emulators) is entirely new.", "Abstract": "The validity of a physical field\u2014a weather state, a fluid flow, a PDE solution\u2014is certified not by how realistic any local region looks but by whether it obeys global conservation laws: total mass, energy, and momentum, and the pointwise continuity/divergence constraints that follow. Recent interpretability breakthroughs show that physics-field emulators (weather models like GraphCast, fluid/PDE surrogates, physics foundation models) contain interpretable features that can be causally steered to induce or suppress local phenomena such as cyclones and vortices, with changes that 'look physically consistent.' We surface and test a behavioral phenomenon these studies never checked: the conservation blind spot. We hypothesize that emulators represent local phenomenology as compact steerable features but do NOT represent the global conservation laws as a steerable handle, so steering a local feature silently breaks the conserved integrals\u2014a failure invisible to local plausibility and per-cell validity checks but exposed by exact conservation oracles (grid-integrated mass/energy/momentum and discrete divergence). Using an open weather emulator (GraphCast-style) and a fluid/PDE surrogate with sparse autoencoders on internal activations, we (1) LOCATE candidate local-phenomenon features and candidate conservation features via probing; (2) CAUSALLY test the steerability of each, contrasting local-phenomenon control against conservation-preserving control; (3) INTERPRET whether located units encode true global conservation or shallow local proxies; and (4) AUDIT reliability, testing whether an intervention-free conservation-consistency signal flags conservation-violating interventions better than local-plausibility checks. We predict local control succeeds, conservation control is decodable-but-weakly-steerable, and a cheap internal audit catches conservation-violating steers\u2014turning a celebrated capability into an auditable reliability question.", "Experiments": "1) MODELS, SAEs, ORACLES: Use two open physics-field emulators with accessible internal activations: (a) a data-driven weather emulator (GraphCast or a smaller reproduction / FourCastNet-style model on ERA5 subsets), and (b) a fluid/PDE surrogate (a Fourier Neural Operator or graph CFD surrogate on 2D Navier-Stokes / advection-diffusion benchmarks). Train TopK (and Ordered/Matryoshka, since the antibody-SAE literature shows TopK features can be decodable-but-inert) SAEs on internal activations at a layer chosen by an intrinsic-dimension heuristic; verify reconstruction. CONSERVATION oracles (exact, cheap, physics-grounded): grid-integrated total mass (or total water / air mass), total energy, total momentum over the domain (or appropriate control volumes), and the pointwise discrete continuity/divergence residual (\u2207\u00b7u for incompressible flow; mass-flux balance for weather). LOCAL-PHENOMENON oracles: detectors for cyclones (vorticity + pressure-minimum trackers), vortices (Q-criterion / vorticity magnitude), atmospheric rivers or diffusion fronts, computed on the field. Validity gates: per-cell physical bounds (non-negative densities, finite values), spectral sanity. First confirm the emulators natively span a range of conserved-integral values and that unsteered rollouts approximately conserve so violation claims are meaningful.\n2) FEATURE BANK & LOCATION: On held-out fields/rollouts, probe SAE features/raw activations for (a) LOCAL-PHENOMENON features (fire on a cyclone/vortex/front, per prior SAE-physics work), and (b) candidate CONSERVATION features (correlate with global integrals\u2014total mass/energy/momentum\u2014or with the divergence residual, controlling for local phenomenology via partial correlation). Report probe AUROC/R^2 for local vs conservation; identify top candidate directions; compare against raw-activation probes; critically test whether global conservation quantities are decodable at all, independent of local structure.\n3) CORE PHENOMENON\u2014THE CONSERVATION BLIND SPOT (local-easy/global-hard): For each local-phenomenon feature, sweep steering strength (add/subtract the direction during a forward step, replicating Physics-Steering/GraphCast-intervention methodology) and, at each level, evolve the field. Measure (i) local-phenomenon gain (did the cyclone/vortex strengthen/weaken as intended?), (ii) CONSERVATION health\u2014drift in total mass/energy/momentum and increase in divergence residual relative to the unsteered rollout, and (iii) per-cell validity/local plausibility. Quantify the blind spot = magnitude of conserved-integral drift per unit local-phenomenon gain; the SILENT-VIOLATION RATE = fraction of local-phenomenon-satisfying, per-cell-valid, locally-plausible steered fields whose global conservation is broken beyond the unsteered baseline; and dose-response. Show invisibility: correlate local-plausibility and per-cell-validity checks with true conservation drift (hypothesis: near-zero\u2014standard eyeball/local checks miss the violation). Random-direction and matched-non-phenomenon-feature controls.\n4) HEAD-TO-HEAD CAUSAL TEST: In the SAME pipeline, calibrate that LOCAL-phenomenon features ARE steerable (phenomenon gain per unit steer, specificity, replicating prior physics-steering results), then test whether ANY compact intervention (TopK/Ordered SAE feature, difference-of-means between high-vs-low-conservation-drift fields, activation patching from conserving rollouts, and a conservation-orthogonalized direction) can RESTORE / hold the conserved integrals fixed while still modifying the local phenomenon\u2014the operational definition of a genuine conservation handle. Report sign, dose-response, specificity; contrast conservation vs local steerability effect sizes. Test whether Ordered/Matryoshka SAEs recover partial conservation steerability that TopK lacks. As a strong baseline, compare against a hard-constraint projection (project the steered field back onto the conservation manifold) to quantify how far interpretable steering is from a physics-guaranteed fix.\n5) INTERPRETATION: Test whether located 'conservation' units encode a true global invariant (invariant to which local phenomenon is present, tracking the integrated quantity) vs shallow local proxies, using controlled field pairs that dissociate global conservation from local structure (same total mass with different local arrangements; same cyclone embedded in globally-conserving vs globally-drifting fields). Auto-label top features (max-activating fields; correlation with the integrated quantity across the domain).\n6) DECISION AUDITING (payoff): Deploy an intervention-free internal CONSERVATION-CONSISTENCY score (conservation-probe read-out / feature coherence computed on the steered activation, before rolling out). Measure whether it flags conservation-violating steers (local-OK, global-broken) better than output-side signals (local plausibility, per-cell validity, spectral sanity): report AUROC/ECE of internal vs output-side detectors, and compute saved by rejecting/re-steering before an expensive multi-step rollout + full conservation evaluation. Emit human-readable diagnoses ('cyclone intensified as requested but total atmospheric mass drifted +2.3%, divergence residual up 5x').\n7) ROBUSTNESS: Repeat across the weather emulator and the fluid/PDE surrogate, TopK vs Ordered SAEs, two layers, and multiple conserved quantities (mass, energy, momentum, divergence); report where the blind spot and (non-)steerability findings are stable vs artifact, and whether violation grows over multi-step rollouts (does a single steered step's conservation error compound?).\nEVALUATION METRICS: conservation-blind-spot magnitude & dose-response and SILENT-VIOLATION RATE (primary phenomenon, via exact grid-integral oracles); local-check-vs-conservation-drift correlation (blind spot); local vs conservation probe AUROC/R^2 (Location); conservation-preserving steering success/specificity vs local-phenomenon steering, and vs hard-constraint-projection baseline, head-to-head effect sizes (Causal Intervention); conservation-feature invariance to local structure (Interpretation); internal-vs-output-side detection AUROC/ECE and rollout compute saved (auditing); multi-step compounding of violation.", "Risk Factors and Limitations": "1) Conservation oracles are EXACT for the discrete grid (integrals and divergence are deterministic sums), a strength; the subtlety is that even unsteered emulators do not perfectly conserve, so we define violation RELATIVE to the unsteered rollout baseline and report both absolute and relative drift, restricting strong claims to drift clearly exceeding baseline. 2) The conservation-non-steerability claim is partly an ABSENCE claim; we mitigate by trying multiple intervention types (TopK/Ordered SAE features, difference-of-means, activation patching, conservation-orthogonalized directions), sweeping strength, and head-to-head calibrating that LOCAL features ARE steerable in the same pipeline\u2014so a null conservation result is meaningful, not a weak-model artifact. A positive result (a genuine steerable conservation handle) is equally publishable and directly useful for building conservation-aware emulators without architectural surgery. 3) The blind spot could be confounded with generic instability from any perturbation; random-direction and matched-non-phenomenon-feature controls, plus comparison to the hard-constraint-projection baseline, isolate the conservation-specific effect. 4) Local phenomenology and global conservation are partly entangled (a large local change must draw from somewhere); the controlled dissociation pairs (step 5) and the divergence-residual metric separate 'model knows mass must be conserved locally' from 'model preserves the global integral', and we report where separation is impossible. 5) Requires emulators with accessible internal activations; scope limited to open, instrumentable models (GraphCast-style, FNO/graph CFD surrogates). 6) SAE quality/layer choice could confound Location; controlled with TopK and Ordered SAEs, multiple layers, raw-activation probes, and random-direction controls. 7) An internal conservation probe might not beat a black-box raw-activation probe on raw AUROC; the interpretability diagnosis (local-steerable, conservation-decodable-but-weakly-steerable) and the audit/compute-saving payoff remain the contributions, reported honestly. 8) If steering preserves conservation out of the box, that is a valuable positive result establishing that interpretable interventions on physics emulators are conservation-safe and that these models robustly represent global invariants."}}
Proposal finalized: {'Name': 'physics_field_conservation_steering', 'Title': 'Steer the Storm, Break the Balance: Do Interpretable Interventions on Physics-Field Emulators Silently Violate Conservation Laws?', 'Short Hypothesis': "Data-driven physics-field emulators (weather models, fluid/PDE surrogates) possess interpretable, causally-steerable features for LOCAL/phenomenological structures (a cyclone, a vortex, a diffusion front), but do NOT possess a compact, causally-steerable representation of the GLOBAL CONSERVATION LAWS (mass, energy, momentum) that certify a field as physical. Consequently, steering a feature to modify a local phenomenon—the exact intervention celebrated in recent physics-steering work—silently breaks the conserved global integrals, a 'conservation blind spot' that local plausibility and per-cell validity checks miss but an exact conservation-integral oracle exposes; and an intervention-free internal conservation-consistency signal flags it.", 'Related Work': "Physics Steering (2025) shows a physics foundation model has single directions causally steering vorticity, diffusion, and simulation speed; the GraphCast SAE paper (2025) finds interpretable features (cyclones, atmospheric rivers, sea-ice) and shows sparse feature modifications yield 'physically consistent' evolving hurricanes; CFD-surrogate SAE work (2025) extracts monosemantic vorticity/flow features; DIANO and flow-matching-interpretability work embed physics into latent spaces. Crucially, EVERY one of these steers or interprets LOCAL, phenomenological structures and asserts the change 'looks physically consistent' by eyeball or per-region metrics—NONE verifies that the intervention preserves the GLOBAL conserved integrals (total mass/energy/momentum, or the discrete divergence/continuity constraint) that actually define physical validity. Separately, conservation-aware ML (physics-informed losses, hard-constraint layers, FlowER for reaction mass balance) treats conservation as an 