Arguments: {"idea": {"Name": "dimensional_consistency_blindspot_symbolic_regression", "Title": "Right Numbers, Wrong Units: Do Neural Symbolic-Regression Models Represent Dimensional Consistency, or Fit Numbers That Silently Violate the Laws of Physics?", "Short Hypothesis": "Transformer-based neural symbolic-regression (NSR) models possess interpretable, causally-steerable internal features for the NUMERICAL fit of a candidate equation (how well it matches data), but do NOT possess a compact, causally-steerable internal representation of DIMENSIONAL CONSISTENCY \u2014 the requirement that added/equated terms carry matching physical units. Consequently, steering a feature to improve numerical fit silently produces dimensionally invalid equations (adding a length to a time, taking log of a dimensioned quantity), a blind spot that R^2/accuracy checks miss but an exact unit-checking oracle exposes; and an intervention-free internal dimensional-consistency signal flags it.", "Related Work": "Transformer/generative symbolic regression is mature: SymbolicGPT (2021), DGSR (2023), DiffuSR (2025), Controllable NSR / NSRwH (2023, which conditions on hypothesized STRUCTURE but not units), and LaSR (2024, learned concept library). Mechanistic interpretability has JUST reached this domain: PATCHES (2026) discovers operator-generating circuits in an SR transformer and finds probing/DLA capture correlational not causal features; closed-form-gradient interpretation (2024) reads symbolic concepts from latent neurons. Separately, dimensional analysis / units-aware discovery is known to matter (Buckingham-Pi-constrained SR, physics-informed SR like StruSR 2025, domain-prior SR 2025), and dimensional consistency is a HARD, exactly-checkable physical law that most black-box SR ignores. Crucially, NO prior work asks whether a neural SR model INTERNALLY represents dimensional consistency as a causal, steerable feature, contrasts fit-steerability against unit-steerability, surfaces the phenomenon that improving fit silently breaks units, or provides an internal dimensional audit. This introduces the numerical-fit vs physical-law-consistency axis into interpretability-of-generation for symbolic/mathematical objects \u2014 a genuinely new object class relative to my prior protein/molecule/DNA/RNA/crystal/reaction/cell proposals \u2014 and turns dimensional analysis (an exact oracle) into a mechanism-and-audit target. It also directly answers PATCHES's call to treat SR as a high-potential interpretability domain, by moving from operator circuits to a physically-meaningful invariant.", "Abstract": "Symbolic regression promises interpretable governing equations from data, and neural symbolic-regression (NSR) transformers now generate candidate equations directly. But a valid physical law must be dimensionally consistent: you cannot add a length to a time, and log/exp require dimensionless arguments. We ask a mechanistic question no prior work addresses: do NSR models internally represent dimensional consistency as a causal, steerable feature the way they represent numerical fit, or do they optimize numbers while silently violating units? We surface a behavioral phenomenon we call the dimensional blind spot: steering an interpretable feature to improve numerical fit reliably lowers error while pushing the generated equation toward dimensional inconsistency \u2014 invisible to R^2/accuracy checks but exposed exactly by unit-checking. Dimensional consistency is the ideal testbed because it is an exact, free, symbolic oracle (propagate SI dimensions through the expression tree; a valid equation has matched units at every operator). Using a transformer NSR model (SymbolicGPT/DGSR-style) trained on the Feynman equations with per-variable units, plus sparse autoencoders on its residual stream, we (1) LOCATE candidate numerical-fit features and candidate dimensional-consistency features via probing; (2) CAUSALLY test the steerability of each, contrasting fit control against unit control; (3) INTERPRET whether located units encode a genuine dimensional-type concept or shallow token statistics; and (4) AUDIT reliability, testing whether an intervention-free dimensional-consistency signal flags silently-invalid equations better than fit or model likelihood. We predict fit is steerable, dimensional consistency is decodable-but-weakly-steerable, and a cheap internal audit catches dimensional violations before downstream physical use.", "Experiments": "1) MODEL, SAEs, ORACLES: Train (or use a public checkpoint of) a transformer NSR model \u2014 SymbolicGPT/DGSR-style, autoregressive over expression-tree tokens \u2014 on the Feynman Symbolic Regression Database (100 physics equations with KNOWN units per variable) augmented with synthetic dimensioned datasets (assign SI units to variables, sample values, compute targets). Train TopK (and Ordered/Matryoshka, since TopK features can be decodable-but-inert) SAEs on the residual stream at a layer chosen by an intrinsic-dimension heuristic; verify reconstruction. DIMENSIONAL oracle (exact, free): a unit-propagation checker that walks the generated expression tree, propagates each variable's SI dimension vector (mass, length, time, ...) through operators (add/subtract require equal dimensions; multiply/divide add/subtract dimension vectors; log/exp/trig require dimensionless argument; the whole equation must match the target's dimension), returning a binary CONSISTENT flag and a graded VIOLATION SCORE (number/severity of mismatched operator nodes). NUMERICAL-FIT oracle: R^2 / normalized MSE of the generated equation against held-out data points. Validity gates: parseable, well-formed expression tree. First confirm the model natively produces a RANGE of both fits and dimensional-consistency states so absence-of-control claims are meaningful.\n2) FEATURE BANK & LOCATION: On held-out (data, equation) pairs, probe SAE features/raw activations for (a) NUMERICAL-FIT features (predict whether the in-progress equation will fit well), and (b) candidate DIMENSIONAL-CONSISTENCY features (predict the running dimension type of the partial expression / whether the next operator will be dimensionally legal, controlling for fit via partial correlation). Report probe AUROC/R^2 for fit vs dimension; identify top candidate directions (SAE feature, difference-of-means between consistent/inconsistent completions, regression-weight direction). Compare against a raw-activation probe (per PATCHES, expect probing to be partly correlational). Critically test whether dimensional-type information is decodable at all, independent of numerical fit.\n3) CORE PHENOMENON \u2014 THE DIMENSIONAL BLIND SPOT (fit-easy/units-hard): For each NUMERICAL-FIT feature, sweep steering strength and generate N equations per level given fixed data. At each level measure (i) fit gain (R^2), (ii) DIMENSIONAL health (consistent flag / violation score), and (iii) well-formedness. Quantify the mirage = increase in dimensional-violation score per unit fit gain, its dose-response, and the SILENT-INCONSISTENCY RATE = fraction of well-formed, better-fitting equations that are dimensionally invalid. Show the blind spot: correlate fit gain and model likelihood with true dimensional consistency (hypothesis: near-zero \u2014 better-fitting equations are no more dimensionally valid; standard SR selection misses it). Random-direction and matched-non-fit-feature controls.\n4) CAUSAL DIMENSIONAL TEST: Steer candidate dimensional-consistency features and activation-patch from dimensionally-consistent runs; test whether we can RESTORE dimensional consistency (lower the violation score / flip to consistent) while HOLDING the numerical fit fixed \u2014 the operational definition of a dimensional handle. Compare SAE-feature steering, difference-of-means directions, and activation patching; report sign, dose-response, specificity. Head-to-head calibrate against fit-feature steerability in the SAME pipeline. Hypothesis: dimensional consistency is decodable but far less steerable than fit (test whether Ordered/Matryoshka SAEs recover partial steerability that TopK lacks).\n5) UNIT INTERPRETATION: Test whether located dimensional units encode a genuine dimensional-TYPE concept (invariant to the specific variables/constants, tracking the abstract SI dimension vector) vs shallow token/operator statistics, using controlled expression pairs that dissociate dimension from surface form (same operators/structure with variables reassigned to different units so consistency flips; different structure with identical dimension type). Auto-label top features via max-activating expression contexts.\n6) DECISION AUDITING (payoff): Deploy an intervention-free internal DIMENSIONAL-CONSISTENCY score (dimension-probe confidence / feature coherence read mid-generation) as an early alarm. Measure whether it flags dimensionally-invalid equations (fit-OK, units-broken) earlier/better than output-side signals (fit, well-formedness, model likelihood): report AUROC/ECE of internal vs output-side detectors and compute saved by pruning dimensionally-invalid candidates from the search beam before running expensive full data-fitting. Emit human-readable diagnoses ('adds a term of dimension L/T^2 to a term of dimension L; violation at node 5'). Test whether using the internal dimensional signal to re-rank/prune the generation beam improves the rate of recovering the TRUE Feynman equation (dimensionally-valid by construction) vs fit-only selection.\n7) ROBUSTNESS: Repeat across two model sizes, TopK vs Ordered SAEs, two SAE layers, autoregressive vs diffusion (DiffuSR-style) NSR, and Feynman vs synthetic dimensioned datasets; report where the blind spot and (non-)steerability findings are stable vs artifact, and whether dimensional steerability is worse for equations requiring transcendental-function dimensionlessness (log/exp/trig) than pure polynomial equations.\nEVALUATION METRICS: dimensional-blind-spot magnitude & dose-response and SILENT-INCONSISTENCY RATE (primary phenomenon, via exact unit-propagation oracle); fit-vs-consistency correlation (blind spot); fit vs dimension probe AUROC/R^2 (Location); dimensional-restoration steering success/specificity vs fit-steering, head-to-head effect sizes (Causal Intervention); dimensional-feature invariance to surface form (Interpretation); internal-vs-output-side detection AUROC/ECE, search compute saved, and true-equation recovery-rate improvement from dimensional re-ranking (auditing); robustness across models/SAEs/datasets.", "Risk Factors and Limitations": "1) Dimensional consistency is an EXACT, non-proxy symbolic oracle (unit propagation is deterministic), which is a core strength; the main proxy is 'physical validity' beyond units, which we deliberately do not claim \u2014 claims concern the objectively-checkable dimensional invariant, not full physical correctness. 2) The dimensional-non-steerability claim is partly an ABSENCE claim; we mitigate by trying multiple intervention types (TopK/Ordered SAE features, difference-of-means, activation patching from consistent runs), sweeping strength, requiring the model to natively span a consistency range, and head-to-head calibrating that FIT features ARE steerable in the same pipeline \u2014 so a null dimensional result is meaningful, not a weak-model artifact. A positive result (a genuine steerable dimensional handle) is equally publishable and directly enables units-aware equation discovery without architectural surgery. 3) Fit and dimensional consistency are partly entangled (the true equation is both well-fitting and consistent); the partial-correlation feature selection and dimension-flipping dissociation pairs (step 5) isolate genuinely fit-independent dimensional signal, and we report where separation is impossible. 4) Some NSR checkpoints do not ingest units at all; we ensure the training data provides per-variable units (Feynman + synthetic) so the model COULD in principle represent dimensions, making the absence claim substantive. 5) SAE quality/layer choice could confound Location; controlled with TopK and Ordered SAEs, multiple layers, raw-activation probes (which PATCHES shows are partly correlational, so we corroborate with causal patching), and random-direction controls. 6) An internal dimensional probe might not beat a black-box raw-activation probe on raw AUROC; the interpretability diagnosis (fit-steerable, dimensions-decodable-but-weakly-steerable, type-concept-vs-token-statistics) and the audit/search-pruning payoff remain the contributions, reported honestly. 7) If no blind spot is found (fit steering preserves dimensional consistency), that is a valuable positive result establishing that NSR feature-steering is dimensionally safe and that these models robustly represent physical units."}}
