fit well), and (b) candidate DIMENSIONAL-CONSISTENCY features (predict the running dimension type of the partial expression / whether the next operator will be dimensionally legal, controlling for fit via partial correlation). Report probe AUROC/R^2 for fit vs dimension; identify top candidate directions (SAE feature, difference-of-means between consistent/inconsistent completions, regression-weight direction). Compare against a raw-activation probe (per PATCHES, expect probing to be partly correlational). Critically test whether dimensional-type information is decodable at all, independent of numerical fit.\n3) CORE PHENOMENON — THE DIMENSIONAL BLIND SPOT (fit-easy/units-hard): For each NUMERICAL-FIT feature, sweep steering strength and generate N equations per level given fixed data. At each level measure (i) fit gain (R^2), (ii) DIMENSIONAL health (consistent flag / violation score), and (iii) well-formedness. Quantify the mirage = increase in dimensional-violation score per unit fit gain, its dose-response, and the SILENT-INCONSISTENCY RATE = fraction of well-formed, better-fitting equations that are dimensionally invalid. Show the blind spot: correlate fit gain and model likelihood with true dimensional consistency (hypothesis: near-zero — better-fitting equations are no more dimensionally valid; standard SR selection misses it). Random-direction and matched-non-fit-feature controls.\n4) CAUSAL DIMENSIONAL TEST: Steer candidate dimensional-consistency features and activation-patch from dimensionally-consistent runs; test whether we can RESTORE dimensional consistency (lower the violation score / flip to consistent) while HOLDING the numerical fit fixed — the operational definition of a dimensional handle. Compare SAE-feature steering, difference-of-means directions, and activation patching; report sign, dose-response, specificity. Head-to-head calibrate against fit-feature steerability in the SAME pipeline. Hypothesis: dimensional consistency is decodable but far less steerable than fit (test whether Ordered/Matryoshka SAEs recover partial steerability that TopK lacks).\n5) UNIT INTERPRETATION: Test whether located dimensional units encode a genuine dimensional-TYPE concept (invariant to the specific variables/constants, tracking the abstract SI dimension vector) vs shallow token/operator statistics, using controlled expression pairs that dissociate dimension from surface form (same operators/structure with variables reassigned to different units so consistency flips; different structure with identical dimension type). Auto-label top features via max-activating expression contexts.\n6) DECISION AUDITING (payoff): Deploy an intervention-free internal DIMENSIONAL-CONSISTENCY score (dimension-probe confidence / feature coherence read mid-generation) as an early alarm. Measure whether it flags dimensionally-invalid equations (fit-OK, units-broken) earlier/better than output-side signals (fit, well-formedness, model likelihood): report AUROC/ECE of internal vs output-side detectors and compute saved by pruning dimensionally-invalid candidates from the search beam before running expensive full data-fitting. Emit human-readable diagnoses ('adds a term of dimension L/T^2 to a term of dimension L; violation at node 5'). Test whether using the internal dimensional signal to re-rank/prune the generation beam improves the rate of recovering the TRUE Feynman equation (dimensionally-valid by construction) vs fit-only selection.\n7) ROBUSTNESS: Repeat across two model sizes, TopK vs Ordered SAEs, two SAE layers, autoregressive vs diffusion (DiffuSR-style) NSR, and Feynman vs synthetic dimensioned datasets; report where the blind spot and (non-)steerability findings are stable vs artifact, and whether dimensional steerability is worse for equations requiring transcendental-function dimensionlessness (log/exp/trig) than pure polynomial equations.\nEVALUATION METRICS: dimensional-blind-spot magnitude & dose-response and SILENT-INCONSISTENCY RATE (primary phenomenon, via exact unit-propagation oracle); fit-vs-consistency correlation (blind spot); fit vs dimension probe AUROC/R^2 (Location); dimensional-restoration steering success/specificity vs fit-steering, head-to-head effect sizes (Causal Intervention); dimensional-feature invariance to surface form (Interpretation); internal-vs-output-side detection AUROC/ECE, search compute saved, and true-equation recovery-rate improvement from dimensional re-ranking (auditing); robustness across models/SAEs/datasets.", 'Risk Factors and Limitations': "1) Dimensional consistency is an EXACT, non-proxy symbolic oracle (unit propagation is deterministic), which is a core strength; the main proxy is 'physical validity' beyond units, which we deliberately do not claim — claims concern the objectively-checkable dimensional invariant, not full physical correctness. 2) The dimensional-non-steerability claim is partly an ABSENCE claim; we mitigate by trying multiple intervention types (TopK/Ordered SAE features, difference-of-means, activation patching from consistent runs), sweeping strength, requiring the model to natively span a consistency range, and head-to-head calibrating that FIT features ARE steerable in the same pipeline — so a null dimensional result is meaningful, not a weak-model artifact. A positive result (a genuine steerable dimensional handle) is equally publishable and directly enables units-aware equation discovery without architectural surgery. 3) Fit and dimensional consistency are partly entangled (the true equation is both well-fitting and consistent); the partial-correlation feature selection and dimension-flipping dissociation pairs (step 5) isolate genuinely fit-independent dimensional signal, and we report where separation is impossible. 4) Some NSR checkpoints do not ingest units at all; we ensure the training data provides per-variable units (Feynman + synthetic) so the model COULD in principle represent dimensions, making the absence claim substantive. 5) SAE quality/layer choice could confound Location; controlled with TopK and Ordered SAEs, multiple layers, raw-activation probes (which PATCHES shows are partly correlational, so we corroborate with causal patching), and random-direction controls. 6) An internal dimensional probe might not beat a black-box raw-activation probe on raw AUROC; the interpretability diagnosis (fit-steerable, dimensions-decodable-but-weakly-steerable, type-concept-vs-token-statistics) and the audit/search-pruning payoff remain the contributions, reported honestly. 7) If no blind spot is found (fit steering preserves dimensional consistency), that is a valuable positive result establishing that NSR feature-steering is dimensionally safe and that these models robustly represent physical units."}

